IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `act-nouns`
IMPORT `act-ch14-interpretation`

-- Tests for act-ch14-interpretation.l4.
-- Every expected value is read from the section named beside the assertion, and was written before the run.

§ `Tests: chapter 14, Interpretation of Acts and statutory instruments`

§§ `Part 14.1: Purpose and scope`

-- s 136: for chapter 14, Act includes a statutory instrument.
#ASSERT `s 136: the kind of document is an Act for chapter 14` `an Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 136: the kind of document is an Act for chapter 14` `a subordinate law` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 136: the kind of document is an Act for chapter 14` `a disallowable instrument` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 136: the kind of document is an Act for chapter 14` `a notifiable instrument` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 136: the kind of document is an Act for chapter 14` `a commencement notice` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 136: the kind of document is an Act for chapter 14` `a statutory instrument of another kind` EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- s 137 (3): the chapter assumes that common law presumptions operate in conjunction with it.
#ASSERT `s 137 (3), (4): the common law presumption operates in conjunction with chapter 14` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 137 (4): subsection (3) also applies to common law presumptions that come into existence after the chapter commenced.
#ASSERT `s 137 (3), (4): the common law presumption operates in conjunction with chapter 14` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 137 (3), (4): the common law presumption operates in conjunction with chapter 14` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Part 14.2: Key principles of interpretation`

-- s 138: working out the meaning of an Act means (a) resolving an ambiguous or obscure provision; (b) confirming or displacing the apparent meaning;
-- (c) finding the meaning when the apparent meaning is manifestly absurd or unreasonable; (d) finding the meaning in any other case.
#ASSERT `s 138: the task is working out the meaning of an Act` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 138: the task is working out the meaning of an Act` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 138: the task is working out the meaning of an Act` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 138: the task is working out the meaning of an Act` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 138: the task is working out the meaning of an Act` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

-- s 139 (1): the interpretation that would best achieve the purpose of the Act is preferred to any other interpretation.
#ASSERT `s 139 (1): the interpretation is to be preferred to any other interpretation` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 139 (1): the interpretation is to be preferred to any other interpretation` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 139 (1): the interpretation is to be preferred to any other interpretation` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 139 (2): the section applies whether or not the Act's purpose is expressly stated in the Act.
#ASSERT `s 139 (2): section 139 applies` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 139 (2): section 139 applies` FALSE

-- s 140: in working out the meaning of an Act, the provisions must be read in the context of the Act as a whole.
-- s 140 Example 1: the commissioner's power in s 22 to exempt 'a person' is read with the long title and s 4, so only holders of pensioner cards.
#ASSERT `s 140: the provisions of the Act must be read in the context of the Act as a whole` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 140 Example 2: the heading of s 6 of the Drug Testing Regulation 2001 indicates the section was made for a definition in the Drug Testing Act 2000.
#ASSERT `s 140: the provisions of the Act must be read in the context of the Act as a whole` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 140 Example 3: the other subsections of s 12 that refer to 'the order' are read as referring to the order mentioned in s 12 (1).
#ASSERT `s 140: the provisions of the Act must be read in the context of the Act as a whole` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 140: the provisions of the Act must be read in the context of the Act as a whole` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 141 (1): in working out the meaning of an Act, material not forming part of the Act may be considered.
#ASSERT `s 141 (1): the material may be considered` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 141 (1): the material may be considered` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 141 (1): the material may be considered` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 141 (2): the three matters that must be taken into account.
#ASSERT `s 141 (2): the matters that must be taken into account` EQUALS LIST "(a) the desirability of being able to rely on the ordinary meaning of the Act, having regard to the purpose of the Act and the provisions of the Act read in the context of the Act as a whole;", "(b) the undesirability of prolonging proceedings without compensating advantage;", "(c) the accessibility of the material to the public."
-- s 141 (3): subsection (2) does not limit the matters that may be taken into account.
#ASSERT NOT `s 141 (3): subsection (2) limits the matters that may be taken into account`
-- s 141 (4): for subsection (2) (c), material in the register is taken to be accessible to the public.
#ASSERT `s 141 (4): the material is taken to be accessible to the public for subsection (2) (c)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 141 (4): the material is taken to be accessible to the public for subsection (2) (c)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Section 142: table 142`

-- s 142 (1), table 142 column 2, item 1: material not forming part of the Act contained in an authorised version of the Act.
#ASSERT `s 142 (1): the material may be considered in working out the meaning of an Act` `item 1: material not forming part of the Act or instrument, contained in an authorised version of it` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 142 (1): the material may be considered in working out the meaning of an Act` `item 1: material not forming part of the Act or instrument, contained in an authorised version of it` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- column 2, items 2 to 6: material presented to the Assembly, or made, before the Act was passed.
#ASSERT `s 142 (1): the material may be considered in working out the meaning of an Act` `item 2: a relevant report of a royal commission, law reform commission, committee of inquiry or other similar entity` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 142 (1): the material may be considered in working out the meaning of an Act` `item 2: a relevant report of a royal commission, law reform commission, committee of inquiry or other similar entity` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 142 (1): the material may be considered in working out the meaning of an Act` `item 3: a relevant report of a committee of the Legislative Assembly` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 142 (1): the material may be considered in working out the meaning of an Act` `item 3: a relevant report of a committee of the Legislative Assembly` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 142 (1): the material may be considered in working out the meaning of an Act` `item 4: an explanatory statement, or other relevant document` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 142 (1): the material may be considered in working out the meaning of an Act` `item 4: an explanatory statement, or other relevant document` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 142 (1): the material may be considered in working out the meaning of an Act` `item 5: a presentation speech` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 142 (1): the material may be considered in working out the meaning of an Act` `item 5: a presentation speech` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 142 (1): the material may be considered in working out the meaning of an Act` `item 6: official reports of proceedings in the Legislative Assembly` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 142 (1): the material may be considered in working out the meaning of an Act` `item 6: official reports of proceedings in the Legislative Assembly` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- column 2, item 7: any relevant treaty or other international agreement to which Australia is a party.
#ASSERT `s 142 (1): the material may be considered in working out the meaning of an Act` `item 7: a relevant treaty or other international agreement to which Australia is a party` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 142 (1): the material may be considered in working out the meaning of an Act` `item 7: a relevant treaty or other international agreement to which Australia is a party` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 142 (2), table 142 column 3, item 1: authorised version of the instrument.
#ASSERT `s 142 (2): the material may be considered in working out the meaning of a statutory instrument` `item 1: material not forming part of the Act or instrument, contained in an authorised version of it` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- column 3, item 2: a relevant report presented to the Assembly (a) if the instrument was presented: before the end of 6 sitting days after the day it was presented; (b) in any other case: before the instrument was made.
#ASSERT `s 142 (2): the material may be considered in working out the meaning of a statutory instrument` `item 2: a relevant report of a royal commission, law reform commission, committee of inquiry or other similar entity` TRUE TRUE FALSE 6 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 142 (2): the material may be considered in working out the meaning of a statutory instrument` `item 2: a relevant report of a royal commission, law reform commission, committee of inquiry or other similar entity` TRUE TRUE FALSE 7 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 142 (2): the material may be considered in working out the meaning of a statutory instrument` `item 2: a relevant report of a royal commission, law reform commission, committee of inquiry or other similar entity` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 142 (2): the material may be considered in working out the meaning of a statutory instrument` `item 2: a relevant report of a royal commission, law reform commission, committee of inquiry or other similar entity` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- column 3, item 3: a relevant report of a committee of the Assembly, the same two cases.
#ASSERT `s 142 (2): the material may be considered in working out the meaning of a statutory instrument` `item 3: a relevant report of a committee of the Legislative Assembly` TRUE TRUE FALSE 1 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 142 (2): the material may be considered in working out the meaning of a statutory instrument` `item 3: a relevant report of a committee of the Legislative Assembly` TRUE TRUE FALSE 8 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 142 (2): the material may be considered in working out the meaning of a statutory instrument` `item 3: a relevant report of a committee of the Legislative Assembly` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 142 (2): the material may be considered in working out the meaning of a statutory instrument` `item 3: a relevant report of a committee of the Legislative Assembly` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- column 3, item 4: if the instrument was presented, an explanatory statement or other relevant document presented before the end of 6 sitting days after the day it was presented.
#ASSERT `s 142 (2): the material may be considered in working out the meaning of a statutory instrument` `item 4: an explanatory statement, or other relevant document` TRUE TRUE FALSE 3 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 142 (2): the material may be considered in working out the meaning of a statutory instrument` `item 4: an explanatory statement, or other relevant document` TRUE TRUE FALSE 9 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 142 (2): the material may be considered in working out the meaning of a statutory instrument` `item 4: an explanatory statement, or other relevant document` TRUE FALSE FALSE 1 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- column 3, item 5: if the instrument was presented by a member of the Assembly, any presentation speech.
#ASSERT `s 142 (2): the material may be considered in working out the meaning of a statutory instrument` `item 5: a presentation speech` TRUE TRUE TRUE 0 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 142 (2): the material may be considered in working out the meaning of a statutory instrument` `item 5: a presentation speech` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- column 3, item 6: if the instrument was presented, official reports of proceedings in relation to the instrument.
#ASSERT `s 142 (2): the material may be considered in working out the meaning of a statutory instrument` `item 6: official reports of proceedings in the Legislative Assembly` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 142 (2): the material may be considered in working out the meaning of a statutory instrument` `item 6: official reports of proceedings in the Legislative Assembly` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- column 3, item 7: any relevant treaty or other international agreement to which Australia is a party.
#ASSERT `s 142 (2): the material may be considered in working out the meaning of a statutory instrument` `item 7: a relevant treaty or other international agreement to which Australia is a party` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Material that is not as the item describes it is not covered by the table.
#ASSERT `s 142 (2): the material may be considered in working out the meaning of a statutory instrument` `item 7: a relevant treaty or other international agreement to which Australia is a party` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 142 (3): this section does not limit the material that may be considered.
#ASSERT NOT `s 142 (3): this section limits the material that may be considered`

§§ `Section 143`

-- s 143 (1): that a relevant law provides stated material may or must be considered does not by implication prevent other material of the same or similar kind being considered.
#ASSERT `s 143 (1): the provision prevents, by implication, other material of the same or similar kind being considered` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 143 (1): the provision prevents, by implication, other material of the same or similar kind being considered` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 143 (2) (a): in working out the meaning of an Act, the relevant law is the Act or another Act.
#ASSERT `s 143 (2): the candidate is a relevant law` `working out the meaning of an Act` `the Act or another Act`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 143 (2): the candidate is a relevant law` `working out the meaning of an Act` `the statutory instrument whose meaning is being worked out`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 143 (2): the candidate is a relevant law` `working out the meaning of an Act` `the statutory instrument under which that instrument was made`)
-- s 143 (2) (b): for a statutory instrument made under an Act, the relevant law is the Act, another Act or the instrument.
#ASSERT `s 143 (2): the candidate is a relevant law` `working out the meaning of a statutory instrument made under an Act` `the Act or another Act`
#ASSERT `s 143 (2): the candidate is a relevant law` `working out the meaning of a statutory instrument made under an Act` `the statutory instrument whose meaning is being worked out`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 143 (2): the candidate is a relevant law` `working out the meaning of a statutory instrument made under an Act` `the statutory instrument under which that instrument was made`)
-- s 143 (2) (c): for a statutory instrument made under another statutory instrument, the relevant law is an Act or either instrument.
#ASSERT `s 143 (2): the candidate is a relevant law` `working out the meaning of a statutory instrument made under another statutory instrument` `the Act or another Act`
#ASSERT `s 143 (2): the candidate is a relevant law` `working out the meaning of a statutory instrument made under another statutory instrument` `the statutory instrument whose meaning is being worked out`
#ASSERT `s 143 (2): the candidate is a relevant law` `working out the meaning of a statutory instrument made under another statutory instrument` `the statutory instrument under which that instrument was made`
